{{! members: formal-methods H2.6f, the members of a version of a family under dal:DeltaMembership.
    Read-only. The patterns name the selective triple first, since an engine that evaluates them in order then never walks the chain for every member. A member is listed by an event at a version w of the chain from
    version back to the nearest checkpoint cp: under the domain's membership
    property (a checkpoint's full list) or by pat:addsMember. It is a member of
    version unless a later version of the chain, nearer to version, drops it, so
    a member dropped and added again is listed by the later add. The nearest
    checkpoint has no other checkpoint between it and version. A version with no
    checkpoint before it has no members, so the first version of the family must
    be one. membershipProperty names the domain's membership property and is a
    request-time parameter, since a family declares none. A domain shape runs
    over these results, never over the stored delta.}}
PREFIX pat: <https://example.org/lattice/patterns#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

SELECT DISTINCT ?member
WHERE {
  GRAPH {{{dataGraph}}} {
    ?cp pat:checkpoint true .
    $version pat:previousVersion* ?cp .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      GRAPH {{{dataGraph}}} {
        ?later pat:checkpoint true ; pat:previousVersion ?y .
        ?y pat:previousVersion* ?cp .
        $version pat:previousVersion* ?later
      }
    }
    $version pat:previousVersion* ?w .
    ?w pat:previousVersion* ?cp .
    { ?w $membershipProperty ?member } UNION { ?w pat:addsMember ?member }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      GRAPH {{{dataGraph}}} {
        ?x pat:dropsMember ?member ; pat:previousVersion ?z .
        ?z pat:previousVersion* ?w .
        $version pat:previousVersion* ?x
      }
    }
  }
}
